## Community Memory

Inference and installation send no telemetry. Users may explicitly create a
redacted contribution with `blum-contribute`. Contributions enter
`Italianhype/Blum-Finance-Memory` in quarantine and never update active weights
without review, versioning and out-of-sample validation.

Incremental learning is explicit opt-in. Accepted, deduplicated contributions
can join a future immutable training snapshot only after provenance, privacy,
schema and quality checks. Each training cycle creates a versioned challenger,
compares it with the active model on an untouched test split and promotes it
only when the release gates pass. A failed challenger is retained as evidence
and cannot replace the active model.

BLUM never trains inside an inference request or lets anonymous input mutate
released weights.

### Use validated memory locally

Install the package shipped with this repository, create a contribution bundle
only after the thesis outcome is known, then import the validated bundle:

```bash
blum-contribute example.json --output contribution.json --consent
blum-memory-add contribution.json
```

Pass `BlumFinanceMemoryStore("~/.blum-finance/memory.jsonl")` to
`BlumFinancePipeline` to retrieve mature point-in-time analogies during local
inference. Retrieval never exposes an outcome that occurred after the new
request timestamp and never presents historical memory as current market fact.

To contribute upstream, add `--push`. This opens a pull request to the quarantine
dataset. There is no background upload, installation tracking or automatic
mutation of released weights. See `CONTRIBUTING.md` for the evidence contract.

